  "title": "The Toulmin Ladder: From Evidence to Warrant",
  "subtitle": "Every strong argument is a stack. Claims do not float — they rest on reasons, which rest on evidence, which rest on warrants you must be able to name.",
  "higherOrderNote": "Higher-order reasoning sits on top",
  "foundationalNote": "Foundational rules hold everything up — skip one and the claim above it collapses",
