      "rule": "Every argument begins with a claim that is debatable, not merely factual.",
      "detail": "A claim must be falsifiable in principle; if no reasonable reader could disagree, you have an observation, not an argument.",
      "example": "\"School start times should move later\" is a claim. \"School starts at 7:45 a.m.\" is not.",
      "accent": "success"
