      "answer": "The move from accusation (“you”) to solidarity (“we”) to shared futurity (“our children”) converts a defensive letter into a coalition offer — the reader is folded into the moral community rather than scolded from outside it.",
      "note": "Ask students to underline the exact sentence where “you” becomes “we” — the pivot is a single clause."
