  "context": "“I had not known it then, but I had never really looked at this woman before… Her hair was black and her eyes were dark and her skin was very dark and she was very beautiful. But I was in love, and I could not see her…”",
  "question": "Baldwin's shift from visual description (“her hair was black… her eyes were dark”) to the admission “I could not see her” is best read as an instance of which rhetorical strategy?",
